Tool blocks always include an `input` field set to `tc.Args`. If a Gemini tool call omits `args`, `tc.Args` will be `nil` and the output becomes `"input":null`, which is inconsistent with other compacted tool blocks (e.g. OpenCode only sets `input` when present) and can be harder for downstream consumers to handle. Consider only adding the `input` key when `tc.Args != nil`.
